Output: -1
Explanation:
There is no matching substring in s.

Example 3:

Input: s = "a", p = "**"
Output: 0
Explanation:
The empty substring is the shortest matching substring.

Example 4:

Input: s = "madlogic", p = "*adlogi*"
Output: 6
Explanation:
The shortest matching substring of p in s is "adlogi".

Constraints:

1 <= s.length <= 10^5
2 <= p.length <= 10^5
s contains only lowercase English letters.
p contains only lowercase English letters and exactly two '*'.

Starter code:

class Solution:
    def shortestMatchingSubstring(self, s: str, p: str) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
Plan: split p into prefix, middle, suffix around the two stars. For each start index i where s[i:] starts with prefix, find the earliest occurrence of middle at position j ≥ i + len(prefix), then the earliest suffix occurrence at k ≥ j + len(middle). The length is k + len(suffix) − i. I'll use str.find for the lookups, with precomputed occurrence lists for efficiency.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-6114", "code": "import bisect\n\nclass Solution:\n    def shortestMatchingSubstring(self, s: str, p: str) -> int:\n        first = p.index('*')\n        second = p.index('*', first + 1)\n        pre = p[:first]\n        mid = p[first + 1:second]\n        suf = p[second + 1:]\n\n        def occurrences(pat):\n            res = []\n            if pat == \"\":\n                return list(range(len(s) + 1))\n            start = 0\n            while True:\n                idx = s.find(pat, start)\n                if idx == -1:\n                    break\n                res.append(idx)\n                start = idx + 1\n            return res\n\n        pre_occ = occurrences(pre)\n        mid_occ = occurrences(mid)\n        suf_occ = occurrences(suf)\n        if not pre_occ or not mid_occ or not suf_occ:\n            return -1\n\n        best = -1\n        lp, lm, ls = len(pre), len(mid), len(suf)\n        for i in pre_occ:\n            # earliest middle occurrence starting at >= i + lp\n            pos = bisect.bisect_left(mid_occ, i + lp)\n            if pos == len(mid_occ):\n                continue\n            j = mid_occ[pos]\n            # earliest suffix occurrence starting at >= j + lm\n            pos2 = bisect.bisect_left(suf_occ, j + lm)\n            if pos2 == len(suf_occ):\n                continue\n            k = suf_occ[pos2]\n            length = k + ls - i\n            if best == -1 or length < best:\n                best = length\n        return best\n"}

