=== MODEL ===
Approach: build a trie over all words, where each node tracks the count of words passing through it. The answer for the full set is the deepest node with count ≥ k. When removing index i, the counts along word i's path drop by 1, so the answer is the max depth over nodes with count ≥ k after the decrement. Since the trie is small (sum of lengths ≤ 10⁵), for each removal I only need to consider the path of word i: the best answer is the max of (a) the global best computed among nodes not on that path, and (b) the best on the path with the decremented count. I'll precompute, per trie node, the maximum depth with count ≥ k within its subtree-style structure using a sorted list of depths keyed by count for a clean O(total length · log) solution.

Simpler correct method: for each removal, the answer equals the maximum depth d such that some trie node at depth d has count (adjusted) ≥ k. Nodes off the removed word's path are unchanged, so I maintain a multiset of depths of nodes with count ≥ k, and for each removal temporarily remove the nodes on that path whose count drops below k.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-1232", "code": "from typing import List\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nclass Solution:\n    def longestCommonPrefix(self, words: List[str], k: int) -> List[int]:\n        n = len(words)\n        if n - 1 < k:\n            return [0] * n\n\n        # Build trie: nodes as list of dicts; depth and count per node\n        children = [dict()]\n        depth = [0]\n        cnt = [0]\n        word_nodes = []  # path node ids for each word (list of node ids, index = depth)\n        for w in words:\n            cur = 0\n            path = [0]\n            cnt[0] += 1\n            for ch in w:\n                nxt = children[cur].get(ch)\n                if nxt is None:\n                    nxt = len(children)\n                    children.append(dict())\n                    depth.append(depth[cur] + 1)\n                    cnt.append(0)\n                    children[cur][ch] = nxt\n                cur = nxt\n                cnt[cur] += 1\n                path.append(cur)\n            word_nodes.append(path)\n\n        # Multiset of depths for nodes with cnt >= k\n        depth_count = defaultdict(int)\n        for node in range(len(children)):\n            if cnt[node] >= k and depth[node] > 0:\n                depth_count[depth[node]] += 1\n\n        def current_max():\n            # largest depth with positive count\n            best = 0\n            for d, c in depth_count.items():\n                if c > 0 and d > best:\n                    best = d\n            return best\n\n        res = []\n        for i in range(n):\n            path = word_nodes[i]\n            # Temporarily decrement counts along path\n            changed = []  # nodes whose \"active\" status changed\n            for node in path:\n                if node == 0:\n                    continue\n                before = cnt[node] >= k\n                cnt[node] -= 1\n                after = cnt[node] >= k\n                if before and not after:\n                    depth_count[depth[node]] -= 1\n                    changed.append(node)\n            res.append(current_max() if n - 1 >= k else 0)\n            # Restore\n            for node in path:\n                if node == 0:\n                    continue\n                cnt[node] += 1\n            for node in changed:\n                depth_count[depth[node]] += 1\n        return res\n"}

