class Solution:
    def shortestMatchingSubstring(self, s: str, p: str) -> int:


=== MODEL ===
Approach: split p by '*' into three parts: prefix, middle, suffix (any may be empty). We need a substring of s starting at i, where s[i:] starts with prefix, then middle occurs at position j >= i+len(prefix), then suffix occurs starting at k >= j+len(middle). The substring spans from i to k+len(suffix), with length minimized.

For efficiency, use Python's `str.find` to locate occurrences: for each occurrence start i of prefix (in order), find the first occurrence of middle at or after i+len(prefix), then the first occurrence of suffix at or after that middle end. Greedily choosing the earliest occurrence of each part for a fixed prefix start minimizes the end, so this gives the shortest for that start. Iterate over all prefix occurrences.

Worst case with many occurrences is O(n * occurrences), but using `find` is fast enough in practice; to be safer I'll precompute occurrence lists with bisect for the middle and suffix.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "T-6114", "code": "import bisect\n\n\nclass Solution:\n    def shortestMatchingSubstring(self, s: str, p: str) -> int:\n        first = p.index('*')\n        second = p.index('*', first + 1)\n        pre = p[:first]\n        mid = p[first + 1:second]\n        suf = p[second + 1:]\n\n        def occurrences(pat):\n            res = []\n            if pat == \"\":\n                return list(range(len(s) + 1))\n            start = s.find(pat)\n            while start != -1:\n                res.append(start)\n                start = s.find(pat, start + 1)\n            return res\n\n        pre_occ = occurrences(pre)\n        mid_occ = occurrences(mid)\n        suf_occ = occurrences(suf)\n\n        if not pre_occ or not mid_occ or not suf_occ:\n            return -1\n\n        best = -1\n        lp, lm, ls = len(pre), len(mid), len(suf)\n        for i in pre_occ:\n            # middle must start at or after i + lp\n            idx = bisect.bisect_left(mid_occ, i + lp)\n            if idx == len(mid_occ):\n                break\n            j = mid_occ[idx]\n            # suffix must start at or after j + lm\n            idx2 = bisect.bisect_left(suf_occ, j + lm)\n            if idx2 == len(suf_occ):\n                continue\n            k = suf_occ[idx2]\n            end = k + ls\n            length = end - i\n            if best == -1 or length < best:\n                best = length\n        return best\n"}

