Starter code:

class Solution:
    def generateString(self, str1: str, str2: str) -> str:


=== MODEL ===
This is the "generate string" problem. Plan:

1. Word length L = n + m - 1. Positions start as unknown.
2. For each 'T' at index i, word[i..i+m-1] must equal str2. Fix those characters; if two conflict, impossible.
3. Remaining unknown positions default to 'a' (lexicographically smallest).
4. For each 'F' at index i, the substring must differ from str2. If all positions in that window are fixed by T constraints (so it already equals str2), impossible. Otherwise, we need to change at least one unfixed position in the window to something other than what it would be. Greedily: set the last unfixed position in the window to 'b' (the smallest letter that avoids equality, since the default is 'a' there). Setting a free position to a non-default letter only at the last free position in the window is the lexicographically minimal way to break equality.

Processing the F-constraints after the T-fixes, with free positions defaulting to 'a' and only bumped to 'b' when needed, gives the smallest valid string. Since bumping to 'b' at a position can affect other F windows, I check each F window against the current state in order, and any later window that was already broken stays broken (changing positions only makes things differ further, and we only set values that were free).

I'll implement this.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "T-8397", "code": "class Solution:\n    def generateString(self, str1: str, str2: str) -> str:\n        n, m = len(str1), len(str2)\n        L = n + m - 1\n        word = [None] * L\n\n        # Apply T constraints\n        for i, c in enumerate(str1):\n            if c == 'T':\n                for j in range(m):\n                    pos = i + j\n                    if word[pos] is None:\n                        word[pos] = str2[j]\n                    elif word[pos] != str2[j]:\n                        return \"\"\n\n        # Fill free positions with 'a' by default\n        for p in range(L):\n            if word[p] is None:\n                word[p] = 'a'\n        free = [False] * L\n        # Track which positions were originally free\n        # (recompute from T constraints)\n        fixed = [False] * L\n        for i, c in enumerate(str1):\n            if c == 'T':\n                for j in range(m):\n                    fixed[i + j] = True\n\n        # Apply F constraints\n        for i, c in enumerate(str1):\n            if c != 'F':\n                continue\n            if word[i:i + m] != list(str2):\n                continue\n            # Need to break equality: change the last non-fixed position in window\n            changed = False\n            for pos in range(i + m - 1, i - 1, -1):\n                if not fixed[pos]:\n                    word[pos] = 'b'\n                    fixed[pos] = True\n                    changed = True\n                    break\n            if not changed:\n                return \"\"\n\n        # Final verification\n        for i, c in enumerate(str1):\n            sub = ''.join(word[i:i + m])\n            if c == 'T' and sub != str2:\n                return \"\"\n            if c == 'F' and sub == str2:\n                return \"\"\n        return ''.join(word)\n"}

