Starter code:

class Solution:
    def longestSpecialPath(self, edges: List[List[int]], nums: List[int]) -> List[int]:


=== MODEL ===
This is a DFS problem. I'll traverse from the root while maintaining the current root-to-node path. For each value, I keep a stack of the depths (prefix distances) where it occurs on the current path. For a node at depth position d (distance from root), the valid downward window starts just after the most recent occurrence of nums[node] on the path. I track the start index of the window with a sliding "left boundary" that only moves forward along the path, and use prefix distances to compute path lengths in O(1).

Implementation: iterative DFS with enter/exit events. On entering node v with parent path length, I record `last[val]` (the path index of the previous occurrence of nums[v] on the current root path), set the boundary `left = max(left, last[val] + 1)`, compute the path from index `left` to the current index, and update the answer as (length, node count) with the tie-break of minimum node count. On exit, restore the boundary and the `last` entry.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-7113", "code": "class Solution:\n    def longestSpecialPath(self, edges: List[List[int]], nums: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n        n = len(nums)\n        adj = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n        for u, v, w in edges:\n            adj[u].append((v, w))\n            adj[v].append((u, w))\n\n        # Path arrays (indexed by depth along current root path)\n        dist_prefix = [0] * (n + 1)   # dist_prefix[i] = distance from root to path node at index i\n        path_val = [0] * (n + 1)\n        last = {}                     # value -> path index of most recent occurrence on current path\n\n        best_len = 0\n        best_nodes = 1  # minimal nodes among longest paths (set when first path considered)\n        first = True\n\n        # Iterative DFS: stack entries (node, parent, depth_index, state)\n        # state 0 = enter, 1 = exit\n        # left_stack keeps the window start to restore on exit\n        stack = [(0, -1, 0, 0)]\n        left_saved = {}\n        left = 0  # smallest path index allowed as start of a special path\n\n        while stack:\n            node, parent, idx, state = stack.pop()\n            if state == 0:\n                val = nums[node]\n                prev = last.get(val, -1)\n                left_saved[node] = (left, prev, val)\n                if prev + 1 > left:\n                    left = prev + 1\n                last[val] = idx\n                path_val[idx] = val\n                # dist_prefix[idx] set by parent when pushing\n                cur_len = dist_prefix[idx] - dist_prefix[left]\n                cur_nodes = idx - left + 1\n                if first:\n                    best_len, best_nodes = cur_len, cur_nodes\n                    first = False\n                elif cur_len > best_len:\n                    best_len, best_nodes = cur_len, cur_nodes\n                elif cur_len == best_len and cur_nodes < best_nodes:\n                    best_nodes = cur_nodes\n\n                stack.append((node, parent, idx, 1))\n                for child, w in adj[node]:\n                    if child == parent:\n                        continue\n                    dist_prefix[idx + 1] = dist_prefix[idx] + w\n                    stack.append((child, node, idx + 1, 0))\n            else:\n                old_left, prev, val = left_saved.pop(node)\n                left = old_left\n                if prev == -1:\n                    del last[val]\n                else:\n                    last[val] = prev\n\n        return [best_len, best_nodes]\n"}

