=== MODEL ===
Approach: sort indices by nums1 value, and process groups of equal nums1 values in increasing order. For each group, the answer for its members is the sum of the top k nums2 values among all strictly smaller nums1 entries seen so far. Maintain a min-heap of size k holding the k largest values, plus a running sum. Before inserting a group, answer every index in the group using the current heap sum; then insert the group's values.

Checking example 1: nums1 = [4,2,1,5,3], nums2 = [10,20,30,40,50], k=2. Sorted by nums1: index 2 (1), index 1 (2), index 4 (3), index 0 (4), index 3 (5). Index 2 gets 0 (empty). Index 1 gets 30. Index 4 gets top 2 of {30,20} = 50. Index 0 gets top 2 of {30,20,50} = 80. Index 3 gets top 2 of {30,20,50,10} = 80. Result [80,30,0,80,50]. Matches.
TOOL submit_solution {"ticket_id": "Q-6630", "code": "from typing import List\nimport heapq\n\nclass Solution:\n    def findMaxSum(self, nums1: List[int], nums2: List[int], k: int) -> List[int]:\n        n = len(nums1)\n        order = sorted(range(n), key=lambda i: nums1[i])\n        answer = [0] * n\n        heap = []  # min-heap of the top-k nums2 values seen so far\n        total = 0\n        i = 0\n        while i < n:\n            j = i\n            # group of equal nums1 values\n            while j < n and nums1[order[j]] == nums1[order[i]]:\n                j += 1\n            for t in range(i, j):\n                answer[order[t]] = total\n            for t in range(i, j):\n                idx = order[t]\n                v = nums2[idx]\n                if len(heap) < k:\n                    heapq.heappush(heap, v)\n                    total += v\n                elif v > heap[0]:\n                    total += v - heapq.heapreplace(heap, v)\n            i = j\n        return answer\n"}

